1. Intended Purpose(s) as defined in instructions of use, technical documentation, and promotional and sales materials, and interpreted as the combination of purpose(s), AI capabilities, and domain(s) as per [9], where purposes are defined as:

a) Purpose(s) for which an AI system was developed (Art.3-3);

b) Purpose(s) for which the AI system was put on the market (Art.3-9);

c) Purpose(s) of data collection for AI systems developed and operated with personal data (Art.10-2b);

2. Involved Entities consisting of:

a) Entities in the role of deployers and providers, and their relation and control regarding the AI system e.g. capacity to update/change (Art.13-3c);

b) Entities acting as ' users ' of the AI system e.g. an immigration officer overseeing an automated passport control service;

c) Entities subjected to the use of AI system e.g. a passenger passing through the automated passport control service (hereafter referred to as 'AI subject' based on the similar 'data subject' under GDPR);

d) along with the Context of AI subjects ' interactions with the AI system - whether they are active/passive, intended/unintended, and informed/uninformed [9];

e) the capacity of users and AI subjects to control the AI system e.g. verify or change the outputs [9];

3. Involved Data consisting of:

a) Input data, including personal data (Art.10-2b and Art.13-3b-vi)

b) Processing of data (Art.10-2c) where ' processing ' includes operations defined in GDPR Art.4-2;

c) Output data, including personal data, and whether it can be classified as profiling and decisions;

d) Data quality (Art.10-2e)

e) Whether personal data involved is of Special Category under GDPR Article 9 (AI Act Art.10-5);

4. Deployment information consisting of:

a) Interactions of the AI system with other systems and components (Anx.IV-1b);

b) Modalities or forms under which the AI system is to be provided and used (Anx.IV-1d);

c) Hardware and software requirements (Art.13e and Anx.IV-1e);

d) User-interface used to operate and manage the AI system (Anx.IV-1g);

e) Duration and Frequency for use of AI system;

5. Provenance of AI system consisting of:

a) How the AI system was developed, including the resources used to develop, train, test and validate the AI system and their provenance (Anx.IV-2a and Anx.IV-2c);

b) 'Datasheets ' describing the training methodologies and techniques and the training data sets used, their provenance, scope and main characteristics; data collection and labelling/cleaning procedures (Anx.IV-2d);

